  "body": "Part of #372 (decision: option 2 - the machine's axis really moves the other way).\n\nAdd a per-axis direction to the machine file (`.mch`), e.g. `\"axes\": { \"x\": { \"direction\": -1 } }` (default +1, so every shipped machine and existing file is unchanged). The CAM side stays right-handed (ISO 841): generation, verification and the stock sim keep working in the standard frame; only what the controller receives changes (sub-issue for the post).\n\n**Done means:** the machine model reads and validates the setting (only +1/-1; anything else refused by name at load); the Machine page shows it as a plain per-axis choice (\"X+ moves: right / left\"); machine-file round-trip; the machine's travel-limit check maps limits correctly through the inverted axis; tests for parse, validate, refuse and travel check.\n",
